.TH ISS-NEXT-PASS 1 "2025-03-01" "iss-next-pass" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iss-next-pass \- find the next visible ISS pass over your location
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python iss_next_pass.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iss-next-pass
predicts when the International Space Station will be visible from a given
location.  It downloads up-to-date TLE orbital elements, computes rise/set
times with Skyfield, checks that the ISS is sunlit while the observer is in
twilight, and estimates apparent magnitude.
.PP
If no location is given, the observer's position is auto-detected from IP
geolocation.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Location Options"
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-location " " \fINAME\fR
Location name (city, address, landmark).  Requires the
.B geopy
library.
.TP
.BR \-\-lat " " \fIDEGREES\fR
Latitude of the observer (\-90 to 90).
.TP
.BR \-\-lon " " \fIDEGREES\fR
Longitude of the observer (\-180 to 180).
.SS "Visibility Options"
.TP
.BR \-\-twilight " " \fIMODE\fR
Sky darkness threshold.  One of:
.BR civil " (\-6 deg, default),"
.BR nautical " (\-12 deg),"
.BR astronomical " (\-18 deg),"
.BR any " (sunset)."
.TP
.BR \-\-min\-magnitude " " \fIMAG\fR
Maximum apparent magnitude to accept.  Lower values are brighter.
Default: 3.0.
.TP
.BR \-\-altitude " " \fIDEGREES\fR
Minimum altitude above the horizon in degrees.  Default: 10.
.SS "Search Options"
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-count " " \fIN\fR
Number of passes to find.  Default: 1.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-days " " \fIN\fR
Number of days to search ahead.  Default: 2.
.SS "Output Options"
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFMT\fR
Output format.  One of
.BR simple " (default),"
.BR table ","
.BR json "."
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show detailed debug information.
.SS "Notification Options"
.TP
.B \-\-setup\-notify
Launch interactive setup for Signal pass notifications.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-notify
Check for upcoming passes and send a notification if one is imminent.
Designed to be called by cron or launchd.
.TP
.BR \-\-notify\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to the notification config JSON file.
Default: \fI~/.config/iss-pass-notify.json\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-launchd
Install a macOS LaunchAgent that runs \fB\-\-check\-notify\fR every 15 minutes.
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall\-launchd
Remove the macOS LaunchAgent.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/iss-pass-notify.json
Notification configuration (location, Signal numbers, twilight mode, window).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/iss-pass-notify/state.json
Tracks which passes have already been notified.  Entries older than 48 hours
are automatically pruned.
.TP
.I ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.iss-pass-notify.checker.plist
macOS LaunchAgent definition created by \fB\-\-install\-launchd\fR.
.TP
.I de421.bsp
JPL planetary ephemeris used for sun position calculations.  Located in the
same directory as the script.
.SH EXAMPLES
Find the next visible pass, auto-detecting location:
.PP
.RS
python iss_next_pass.py
.RE
.PP
Search by city name and show 5 passes in a table:
.PP
.RS
python iss_next_pass.py \-\-location "London" \-\-count 5 \-\-format table
.RE
.PP
Use coordinates with a wider search window:
.PP
.RS
python iss_next_pass.py \-\-lat 48.8566 \-\-lon 2.3522 \-\-days 7
.RE
.PP
Set up Signal notifications:
.PP
.RS
python iss_next_pass.py \-\-setup\-notify
.RE
.PP
Install periodic checks via launchd:
.PP
.RS
python iss_next_pass.py \-\-install\-launchd
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid arguments, network failure, missing config, geocoding failure).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR signal-cli (1),
.BR launchd.plist (5)
